  "chapter": {
    "number": 2,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "My son, if you will receive the utterance of my commandment, and hide it with you;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "your ear shall listen to wisdom; you shall also apply your heart to understanding, and shall apply it to the instruction of your son."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          "For if you shall call to wisdom, and utter your voice for understanding;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          "and if you shall seek it as silver, and search diligently for it as for treasures;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "then shall you understand the fear of the Lord, and find the knowledge of God."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "For the Lord gives wisdom; and from his presence come knowledge and understanding,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "and he treasures up salvation for them that walk uprightly: he will protect their way;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "that he may guard the righteous ways: and he will preserve the way of them that fear him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "Then shall you understand righteousness, and judgment; and shall direct",
          {
            "noteId": 5
          },
          "all your course aright."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "For if wisdom shall come into your understanding, and discernment shall seem pleasing to your soul,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          "good counsel shall guard you, and holy understanding shall keep you;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          "to deliver you from the evil way, and from the man that speaks nothing faithfully."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          "Alas for those who forsake right paths, to walk in ways of darkness;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "who rejoice in evils, and delight in wicked perverseness;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          "whose paths are crooked, and their",
          {
            "noteId": 6
          },
          "courses winding;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          "to remove you far from the straight way, and to estrange you from a righteous purpose. My son, let not evil counsel overtake you,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          "of her who has forsaken the instruction of her youth, and forgotten the covenant of God."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          "For she has fixed her house near death, and guided her wheels near Hades with the",
          {
            "noteId": 7
          },
          "giants."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          "None that go by her shall return, neither shall they take hold of right paths, for they are not apprehended of the",
          {
            "noteId": 8
          },
          "years of life."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          "For had they gone in good paths, they would have found the paths of righteousness",
          {
            "noteId": 9
          },
          "easy."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          "For the upright shall dwell in the earth, and the holy shall be left behind in it."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          "The paths of the ungodly shall perish out of the earth, and transgressors shall be driven away from it."
        ]
      }
    ],
